INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-78e8f2b5', 't-mm-01-001', 'html', '<h3><strong>© 2026 Dr. Farzana</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>All rights reserved. No part of this publication may be</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>reproduced without written permission of the publisher.</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>This book is intended for educational purposes only</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>and does not substitute professional medical advice.</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>First Edition 2026</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Printed in Pakistan</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Compiled, typed, and formatted by</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Umer Farooq</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>For academic correspondence:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>umrr8farooq@gmail.com</strong><strong> </strong></h3>
<h3><strong>DEDICATION</strong></h3>
<h3><strong> </strong><strong>I dedicate this book to all the resilient mothers who strive to balance their careers and ongoing professional growth amidst the chaos of daily life and family responsibilities. I would also like to acknowledge my wonderful husband, whose unwavering support and encouragement lifted my spirits during my lowest moments. It is thanks to his steadfast assistance that I have been able to accomplish this significant endeavor. I am deeply grateful to my parents and my cherished children, whose joyful smiles inspire me and provide the motivation to keep pushing forward.</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>      </strong><strong>   DR FARZANA MUNEER</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>AUTHOR DECLARATION</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>I declare that this book is my original work and has not</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>been published elsewhere. All sources have been duly</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>acknowledged. There is no conflict of interest.</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Preface</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Dear Colleagues and Fellows,</strong></h3>
<p>This book is a humble effort born from a desire to see my peers excel. As I share this work with you, I also share a piece of my own journey—one defined by persistence, sacrifice, and the pursuit of excellence. As a mother of three wonderful children, balancing the demands of family life with the rigors of medical specialization was a formidable challenge. However, I never lost hope. I kept pushing forward until I reached the point where I could finally compile my experiences and knowledge into this volume.</p>
<p>After graduating and earning the prestigious <strong>FCPS</strong> degree, I felt that a new pinnacle of achievement was still waiting for me. This led me to embark on the journey toward the <strong>MRCOG</strong>. During my preparation, I realized that the available study material was often haphazard, fragmented, and lacked a cohesive structure. Lengthy topics remained unsummarized, and many resources failed to integrate the latest guidelines and recommendations.</p>
<p>I recognized the urgent need for a single, concise resource—one that eliminates the need to juggle multiple files while ensuring no critical point is missed. <strong>Ma</strong><strong>ternal </strong><strong>mind</strong> is designed to be that ideal companion. By utilizing specialized flowsheets, I have distilled complex, lengthy topics into single-page summaries, making them easier to memorize and, more importantly, easier to reproduce under exam conditions.</p>
<p>In the end, I want to thank you for choosing this book. It is my sincere hope that this labor of love serves as a clear guide through your own professional journey, helping you reach your goals with confidence and clarity.</p>
<h3><strong>Dr. Farzana Muneer</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Contributors</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Dr. Mahreen Yusuf</strong></h3>
<p>FCPS, MRCOG</p>
<p>Consultant Obstetrician and Gynaecologist</p>
<h3><strong>Dr. Ambreen Yasin</strong></h3>
<p>FCPS, MRCOG</p>
<p>Specialty Doctor, NHS (UK)</p>
<h3><strong>Dr. Masooma Sabee</strong><strong>m</strong></h3>
<p>FCPS, MRCOG</p>
<p>Consultant Obstetrician and Gynaecologist</p>
