lear documentation.-  Preformatted proformas may be used.</strong><strong>Clinical management plan:</strong>-  Ensure clear documentation.-  Preformatted proformas may be used.<strong>Clinical management plan:</strong>-  Ensure clear documentation.-  Preformatted proformas may be used.<strong>Woman with FGM in pregnancy:Referral to designated midwife and/or obstetrician with responsibility for FGM Consultant-led careWoman with FGM in pregnancy:Referral to designated midwife and/or obstetrician with responsibility for FGM Consultant-led care</strong><strong>Woman with FGM in pregnancy:</strong>Referral to designated midwife and/or obstetrician with responsibility for FGM Consultant-led care<strong>Woman with FGM in pregnancy:</strong>Referral to designated midwife and/or obstetrician with responsibility for FGM Consultant-led care<strong>Data recording:-  Ensure compliance with HSCIC Enhanced Dataset.-  Document FGM diagnosis, including FGM type (WHO classification).Data recording:-  Ensure compliance with HSCIC Enhanced Dataset.-  Document FGM diagnosis, including FGM type (WHO classification).</strong><strong>Data recording:</strong><strong>-  </strong>Ensure compliance with HSCIC Enhanced Dataset.-  Document FGM diagnosis, including FGM type (WHO classification).<strong>Data recording:</strong><strong>-  </strong>Ensure compliance with HSCIC Enhanced Dataset.-  Document FGM diagnosis, including FGM type (WHO classification).<strong>Child safeguarding risk assessment by midwife or obstetrician:-  Use risk assessment tool-  Explain law on FGM-   Report to social services or the police if unborn child or related child at risk.Child safeguarding risk assessment by midwife or obstetrician:-  Use risk assessment tool-  Explain law on FGM-   Report to social services or the police if unborn child or related child at risk.</strong><strong>Child safeguarding risk assessment by midwife or obstetrician:</strong>-  Use risk assessment tool-  Explain law on FGM-   Report to so