INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-3b0c1741', 't-mm-02-011', 'html', '<ul><li>30 – 40%</li><li>Subfertility despite normal ovulation, tubal test and semen analysis.</li><li>Prognosis</li><li>Age of female (single best predictor).</li><li>Previous obstetric history.</li><li>Duration of subfertility.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Contributing factors:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em> </em><em><strong>Ovarian Reserve</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>Age &gt;35 years.</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>Life style.</strong></em></li><li>Smoking:</li><li>in female:   Ovarian reserve</li><li>Affect tubal function.</li><li>Alter uterine environment.</li><li>In male :  impair fertilization capacity of sperm</li><li>DNA Damage and mitochondrial activity</li><li>Weight:</li><li>Suboptimal embryo</li><li>Impairs ovulation</li><li>DNA damage in sperm</li><li>Libido, Erectile dysfunction</li><li>Alcohol:</li><li>Implantation</li><li>Luteal phase defect</li><li>Abnormal embryo development</li><li><em><strong>Tubal function defects:</strong></em></li><li>Mild gonorrhea, chlamydia can cause ciliary function defect despite patent tubes</li><li><em><strong>Fertilization defects:</strong></em></li><li>5 – 25%</li><li>Abnormal acrosome</li><li>Poor/absent binding with zona pellucida</li><li>DNA damage</li><li>High DNA fragmentation on – abnormal fertilization miscarriage</li><li><em><strong>Implantation defects:</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>Immunologic, Metabolic &amp; genetic defects:</strong></em></li><li>Anti-thyroid, anti-nuclear, Anti-ovarian, anti-smooth muscles antibodies, APLs – are associated with unexplained subfertility,</li><li><em><strong>Endometriosis.</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>Fibroids.</strong></em></li><li><em><strong>Aden</strong></em><em><strong>omyosis.  </strong></em></li></ul>
<h3><strong>Investigations:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Detection of ovulation:</li><li>Urinary LH.</li><li>Mid luteal progesterone</li><li>Follicular tracking</li><li>Detection of tubal patency:</li><li>HSG</li><li>Saline sonography.</li><li>Laparoscopy</li><li>Semen analysis.</li><li>Pelvic USG &amp; Saline infusion.</li><li>Ovarian reserve testing.</li><li>Laparoscopy in symptomatic Pts.</li><li>Hysteroscopy in known uterine anomalies.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Treatment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em><strong>Expectant:</strong></em> 74% success.</li><li>Tubal flushing/perturbation: oil soluble increase pregnancy rate.</li><li><em><strong>CC:</strong></em> No benefit.</li><li><em><strong>IUI:</strong></em></li><li>With or without ovarian stimulation.</li><li>10% multiple pregnancies.</li><li>IVF = 12.2%.</li><li>unstimulated IUI = 7.4%</li><li>Stimulated IUI= 8.7%</li><li><em><strong>IVF:</strong></em> cost effective as compared to multiple IUI cycles WITH more pregnancy rates.</li><li><em><strong>ICSI:</strong></em> 5 – 25% couples have no fertilization in IVF.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Unexplained Subfertility</strong></h3>
<p>&lt;35 years  36 – 39 years           &gt;39 years</p>
<ul><li>2 years&gt; 1 yearsirrespective of Duration</li></ul>
<p>IVF       IVF   IVF</p>', 5) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
