ortic lymphadenectomy. <strong>BOT</strong> =&gt; Staging laparotomy by oncologist/ Gynaecologist according to MDT review.<strong>Cyst Aspiration:</strong>25% sensitivity of cytological examinationTo control symptoms if Pt is unfit for surgery.25% recurrence in 1 year after aspiration.New 2025 Update:Simple, unilateral, unilocular, Cystic lesion of &lt; 3cm do not require routine follow up. <strong>MDT Review</strong>High likelihood Of malignancy ofOvary<strong>Laparotomy </strong><strong>Staging by </strong><strong>Oncologist include:</strong>1. laparotomy with clear documentation.2. cytology of washing/Ascites3.TAH + BSO + omentectomy.4. Biopsy from suspicious areas.5. may include pelvic/abdomen, para-aortic lymphadenectomy. <strong>BOT</strong> =&gt; Staging laparotomy by oncologist/ Gynaecologist according to MDT review.<strong>Cyst Aspiration:</strong>25% sensitivity of cytological examinationTo control symptoms if Pt is unfit for surgery.25% recurrence in 1 year after aspiration.New 2025 Update:Simple, unilateral, unilocular, Cystic lesion of &lt; 3cm do not require routine follow up. Asymptomatic</li><li>Any of 1 feature Any of 1 feature Any of 1 feature Any of 1 feature Simple</li><li>Unilocular</li><li>Low likelihood of ovarian malignancyLaparotomy by trained GynaecologistLow likelihood of ovarian malignancyLaparotomy by trained GynaecologistLow likelihood of ovarian malignancyLaparotomy by trained GynaecologistLow likelihood of ovarian malignancyLaparotomy by trained Gynaecologist&gt;3cm - &lt; 5cm</li><li>Unilateral</li></ul>
<p>Consider conservative</p>
<p>Treatment</p>
<p>Reassessment after</p>
<p>4 – 6m0 with TVS</p>
<p>&amp; CA – 125.</p>
<p>Change in features.Change in features.Change in features.Change in features.- Persistent- unchangedRepeat assessment in 4 – 6m0.- Persistent- unchangedRepeat assessment in 4 – 6m0.- Persistent- unchangedRepeat assessment in 4 – 6m0.- Persistent- unchangedRepeat assessment in 4 – 6m0.</p>
