<h3><strong>Follow up:</strong></h3>
<p>Examination + TVS.</p>
<ul><li>3 monthly for 2yrs.</li><li>6 monthly for next 2yrs.</li><li>Annually – after wards</li></ul>
<p>-</p>
<h3><strong>carry out Frozen section where possible:</strong></h3>
<p>1/3rd invasive on H/P.</p>
<p>Referral to oncology MDT</p>
<h3><strong>Restaging </strong></h3>
<p><strong>Recurrence</strong> :8 – 73%.</p>
<h3><strong>Relapse:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>with invasive implants – 21% over 5 years.</li><li>with non – invasive implants 2%.</li></ul>
<p>DNA aneuploidy 19-fold     in invasive implants.</p>
<ul><li>12 – 58% after cystectomy.</li><li>0 – 20% after USO/BSO.</li><li>2.5 – 5.7% after completion surgery.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Restaging</strong><strong> depends upon</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Aneuploidy status – DNA.</li><li>Micro papillary status.</li><li>Invasive implants.</li><li>No fertility concerns.</li><li><strong>Fertility in BOT:</strong></li></ul>
<p>Conservative Treatment.</p>
<ul><li>Spontaneous conception: 32 – 65%.</li><li>OI: 13 – 29%.</li><li>OI only in stage 1 disease for limited cycles.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>OI = ovulati</strong><strong>on</strong></h3>', 3) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, "order", is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-03-008', 'chap-mm-03-01', '8.RISK REDUCING SURGERY FOR WOMEN @ RISK OF EPITHELIAL TUMOR', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 8.RISK REDUCING SURGERY FOR WOMEN @ RISK OF EPITHELIAL TUMOR.', 8, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, description=EXCLUDED.description, is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-7b5fe5aa', 't-mm-03-008', 'html', '<ul><li><em><strong>Protective factors:</strong></em></li><li>COC:</li><li>20%   after 5 years of use.</li><li>50%    after 15 years of use</li><li>Effect last for 30 years after cessation.</li><li>Hysterectomy 34%    in risk</li><li>Tubal ligation 34%    in risk</li><li>Ligation + COC = 72%     ed in risk</li><li>BRCA + tubal ligation = 60%</li><li>B.F over 12m0   risk.</li><li><em><strong>Risk Factors:</strong></em></li><li>Fx strongest factor – present in 10 – 15%.</li><li>1 member affected = 4 – 5%.</li><li>2 members affected = 7%.</li><li>General population =1.7%</li></ul>
<h3><strong>HereditaryBreast CancerSyndrome HereditaryBreast CancerSyndrome </strong>HereditaryBreast CancerSyndrome HereditaryBreast CancerSyndrome <strong>Breast CA Herediar</strong><strong>y syndromes</strong></h3>
<ul><li>BRCA 1=35 – 46%90% Of heredity.</li><li>BRCA  2=13 – 23%cancers</li><li>Lynch Syndrome 3 – 14%.</li><li>HNPCC = 1%</li><li>Puetz – Jagher – 20%</li><li><strong>OTHER</strong><strong> RISK FACTORS</strong></li><li>Ovulation induction – BOT.</li><li>Endometriosis.</li><li>Obesity.</li><li>PCOD.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Screening NR Routinely:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Predictive value 3%.</li><li>Undertaken in women who decline Risk Reducing surgery.</li><li>TVS + CA -125 every 6m0 from 35 years of age.</li><li>Or 5 – 10 years earlier than earliest age of 1st diagnosis of ovarian CA in family.</li></ul>
<p>10% risk of CA ovary go for =&gt; rrBSO.</p>
<p>30% risk of CA Breast go for =&gt; risk reducing Mastectomy.</p>
<h3><strong>Risk of ovarian CA:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>1.</strong><strong> </strong><strong>Increas</strong><strong>ed Risk</strong></h3>
<ul><li>positive Fx</li><li>single member 4 – 5%.</li><li>2 members 7%.</li><li>General population 1.7%.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>2.</strong><strong>High risk</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Hereditary cancers in Family</li><li>Referral to Geneticists + screening of BRCA or HNPCC.</li><li>Ovarian Risk = 13 – 50%.</li><li><strong>BRCA 1</strong> = 35 – 46%.</li><li><strong>BRCA 2</strong> = 13 – 23%.</li></ul>
<p><strong>HNPCC &amp; lynch</strong> 3 – 14%.</p>
<h3><strong>Suggested Management:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>1.Increase</strong><strong>d Risk</strong><strong> group</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>No screening</li><li>Consider risk reducing BSO (rrBSO) on individualized consideration involving Pt &amp; Clinician.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>2.</strong><strong>High Risk</strong><strong> group</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>No screening except those who decline rrBSO.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>BRCA – 1:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Offer rrBSO @ 35 years when child bearing is completed</li><li>Protective effect on CA Breast (risk reduction is 30 – 75% in CA Breast).</li></ul>
<h3><strong>BRCA – 2:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>rrBSO after 35 years can be delayed up till 45 years but delay would lose the benefit of risk reduction in CA Breast.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>HNPCC &amp; Lynch:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bowel = 40 – 60%.</li><li>Ovary = 10 – 20%.</li><li>Uterus = 40 – 60%.</li><li>rrBSO + TAH due to risk of Endometrial CA 40 – 60%.</li><li>Chemoprevention Aspirin from 16 years of age.</li><li>Colonoscopy every 2 years after 25 – 30 years.</li><li>H – pylori testing after HNPCC positive</li><li>Role of PGD.</li><li>Role of PND.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Risk Reducing Surgery:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>rrBSO recommended:</li><li>30 – 75% reduction in CA Breast.</li><li>2% risk of primary peritoneal cancer.</li><li>Salpingectomy – if ovaries need to be preserved.</li><li>Radical Fimbriectomy – if Pt refuses BSO.</li><li>Removal of fimbria at ovarian junction.</li><li>Concurrent TAH is recommended when:</li><li>Lynch syndrome</li><li>Prophylactically, if chemo is required for CA Breast (tamoxifen)</li><li>When ERT is given for hormone replacement purpose,(progesterone increase risk of CA Breast).</li><li>Mastectomy</li><li>Progesterone is avoided in HRT as it     es risk of CA breast.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Chemoprevention:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Pt with hereditary ovarian cancer syndrome who have not elected for rrBSO or are trying to conceive.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Pre – Op Evaluation before rrBSO:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Occult Malignancy 4 – 8%.</li><li>Rule out occult malignancy by TVS and CA – 125.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Surgical Procedure:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>BSO by removing all ovarian and tubal tissue except intramyometrial part.</li><li>ligate ovarian Artery 2cm away from ovary @ pelvic brim.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Menopause and HRT:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Recommended.</li><li>HRT up to 51 years.</li><li>Small   in CA Breast but low overall and no impact on mortality.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Factors to reduce CA Breast on HRT:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Concurrent TAH.</li><li>Mastectomy.</li><li>Limiting use of HRT.</li><li>BRCA – 1 Carrier has CA Breast that is typically E and P receptor negative.</li><li>BRCA – 2 carriers are usually positive.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Recovery:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>After BSO – 3M0.</li><li>Mastectomy – 3m0.</li></ul>', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, "order", is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-03-009', 'chap-mm-03-01', '9.OVARIAN CANCER', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 9.OVARIAN CANCER.', 9, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, description=EXCLUDED.description, is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-7bed8997', 't-mm-03-009', 'html', '<p>S/S =&gt; IBS symptoms over 12m0.</p>
<ul><li>Persistent abdominal pain/pelvic pain</li><li>Feeling full/loss of appetite.</li><li>Abd distention bloating.</li><li>Urinary urgency and/or frequency.</li><li>Unexplained weight loss.</li><li>Identification of Ascites, Abd/Pelvic Mass on Examination =&gt; urgent referral, to carry out testing</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Testing</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>CA – 125 </strong><strong>in</strong><strong> P</strong><strong>0 </strong><strong>care.</strong></h3>
<ul><li><strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.TVS in P0 – CARE &gt; 35 IU/ml.TVS in P0 – CARE </strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.<strong>TVS</strong><strong> in P</strong><strong>0 </strong><strong>– CARE </strong>&gt; 35 IU/ml.<strong>TVS</strong><strong> in P</strong><strong>0 </strong><strong>– CARE </strong></li></ul>
<p>Normal</p>
<ul><li>NormalNormalNormalNormal<strong>Suggest cancer =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CANeoadjuvant Chemo after:Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.Suggest cancer =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CANeoadjuvant Chemo after:Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.</strong><strong>Suggest cancer</strong> =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CA<strong>Neoadjuvant</strong><strong> Chemo after:</strong>Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.<strong>Suggest cancer</strong> =&gt; RMI calculationUSG abdomen + pelvisCT if USG suggests CA<strong>Neoadjuvant</strong><strong> Chemo after:</strong>Tissue Diagnosis:Percutaneous image guided biopsyLaparoscopy Guided.cytology if H/P not appropriate.</li><li>Assessment</li></ul>
<p>carefully.</p>
<ul><li>rule out causes</li></ul>
<p>of symptoms.</p>
<ul><li>return to GP if</li></ul>
<p>symptoms become</p>
<p>frequent/ persistent.</p>
<h3><strong>Treatment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Surgery – full staging</li><li>Lymph node assessment, lymph node dissension</li><li>Adjuvant Chemo:</li><li>Stage I:</li><li>Grade 1 &amp; 2, Ia, Ib not recommended.</li><li>Grade 3, Ic recommended.</li><li>6 cycles of carboplatin.</li><li>Discuss Adjuvant chemo in stage I that is not optimally staged.</li></ul>', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-e3579c77', 't-mm-03-009', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>SATGE I:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>MANAGEMENT</strong></td><td><strong>5 YEARS </strong><br/><strong>SURVIVAL</strong></td><td><strong>1 YEAR</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Limited to 1 ovary capsule intact =&gt;</td><td><em><strong>Fertility </strong></em><em><strong>sparing</strong></em><em><strong> can be consisted in young:</strong></em></td><td>90%<br/>80%</td><td>98%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Limited to both ovaries capsule intact</td><td><strong>Stating Laparotomy:</strong><br/>TAH + BSO<br/>Evaluation of all peritoneal surfaces<br/>Washings for cytology<br/>Multiple peritoneal biopsies.<br/>Omentectomy.<br/>Pelvic/para – aortic LN biopsies.<br/>Hepatic/ diaphragmatic cytology.<br/><em><strong>Cytoreductive</strong></em><em><strong> surgery:</strong></em> Residual disease<br/>&lt; 1cm.<br/><em><strong>Chemotherapy:</strong></em> carboplatin + paclitaxel = 6 cycles.<br/><em><strong>Main sta</strong></em><em><strong>y</strong></em><em><strong> of treatment:</strong></em> surgery + chemo except stage 1A,1B, low grade</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>1: 1A/1B with surgical spill<br/>2: 1A/1B with ruptured capsule before surgery or tumor on surface.<br/>3: 1A/1B but malignant cells in ascites or peritoneal washings.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE II:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>  </strong>            <strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Implants on surface of uterus, tubes, ovary.</td><td>Surgery: + Adjuvant therapy according to MDT decision.<br/>Surgery: + Neoadjuvant or adjuvant therapy according to MDT decision.</td><td>70%</td><td>89%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Other pelvic organs Bladder, rectum.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>IIA, IIB with ascites or peritoneal washings positive</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE III:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><strong>1</strong><br/><strong> A</strong><strong>2</strong><br/><strong>B</strong><br/><strong>C</strong></td><td>Positive Retroperitoneal Lymph nodes<br/><strong>III</strong><em><strong>A</strong></em><em><strong>1</strong></em><em><strong>a</strong></em><em><strong>:</strong></em> &lt;10mm Mets<br/><em><strong>IIIA</strong></em><em><strong>1b</strong></em><em><strong>:</strong></em> &gt; 10mm Mets – peritoneal Mets</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>40%</td><td>73%</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Microscopic extra pelvic peritoneal invasion + positive retroperitoneal Lymph nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Macroscopic &lt; 2cm extra pelvic peritoneal Mets + positive retroperitoneal Lymph nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Extra pelvic peritoneal Mets &gt;2cm Macroscopic, positive retroperitoneal L nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Extension to liver/spleen capsule abdominal organs – No parenchymal involvement.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>STAGE: IV</strong></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A</strong><br/><strong>B  </strong></td><td>Plural effusion with + ive cytology.</td><td>Neoadjuvant followed by surgery according to MDT decision</td><td>20%</td><td>53%<br/>Un stage – 67%.<br/>Unknown stage = 53%.</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Hepatic, splenic parenchymal Mets.<br/>Mets to extra abdominal organs.<br/>inguinal L nodes.</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET 