INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-71c869e1', 't-mm-03-009', 'html', '<p>Table 7. CA OVARY</p>
<h3><strong>E </strong><strong>secreting</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Granulosa cell tumors</li><li>Thecoma</li><li>50% estrogenic</li><li>40% non-functional</li><li>20% androgenic</li><li>Sertoli cell</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Androgen Secreting</strong>:</h3>
<ul><li>Andro blastoma</li><li>Adrenal like</li><li>Gonad blastoma</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Stage II, IV:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Either surgery F/B adjuvant</li><li>Or neoadjuvant.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Relapse:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Platinum sensitive- Relapse after 12m0</li><li>of completion of t/m</li><li>Partial sensitive- Between 6 – 12m0</li><li>of completion.</li><li>Resistant - &lt; 6m of completion</li><li>Refractory- Within 4 weeks or</li></ul>
<p>during treatment</p>
<p>Complete RESPONSE = 4 weeks of treatment</p>
<p><strong>Chemo:</strong>   es risk of Pre – term labour</p>
<p><strong>Radio:</strong>   es risk of miscarriage, still birth and IUGR.</p>
<h3><strong>pulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppressionpulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppression</strong>pulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppressionpulmonary fibrosisHand foot syndrome, cerebellar AtaxiaNeuropathycardiac failure Hemorrhagic cystitis.Nephrotoxic, deafness.Bone marrow suppression.Neurotoxicity.Bone marrow toxicityMylo suppression<strong>Toxicity of Chemo</strong><strong>therapy</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bleomycin</li><li>5 – fluorouracil</li><li>Paclitaxel</li><li>Doxorubicin</li><li>Cyclophosphamide</li><li>Cisplatin</li><li>Methotrexate</li><li>Vincristine</li><li>Vinblastine</li><li>Carboplatin</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Chemotherapy MOA:</strong></h3>
<p><strong>Fluor</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>uracil</strong><strong>:</strong> - inhibition of thymidylate synthase.</p>
<p><strong>Bleomyc</strong><strong>in:</strong> cause single stranded synthesis of DNA.</p>
<p><strong>Paclitaxe</strong><strong>l:</strong> prevention of microtubule assembly</p>
<p><strong>Doxo</strong><strong>rubicin</strong><strong>:</strong> Topoisomerase II inhibiter.</p>
<p><strong>Ifos</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>amide:</strong> Alkylating agent.</p>
<p><strong>Cisplatin:</strong> crosslink DNA inhibition</p>
<h3><strong>P</strong><strong>0</strong><strong> concern of comorbidities</strong><strong> before starting chemotherapy</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Bleomycin – COPD.</li><li>5 Fluorouracil – IHD.</li><li>Taxanes – Diabetes.</li><li>anthracyclines – CCF.</li><li>Methotrexate – plural effusion, Metho pools in 3rd space causing toxicity.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Paclitaxel:</strong> Given with oral dexamethasone, 20mg, 6-12 hours prior to avoid hypersensitivity reactions, It impairs blood glucose, so used with caution</p>
<p><strong>Cisplatin:</strong> pre and post hydration.</p>
<p><strong>Bleomycin:</strong> don’t cause myelosuppression.</p>
<p><strong>Etoposide:</strong> Both oral and I/V.</p>
<p><strong>Carboplatin:</strong> dosed acc to creatinine levels</p>
<h3><strong> </strong><strong>BRCA Gene:</strong></h3>', 3) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
