<h3><strong>Vault Prolapse:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Prophylaxis</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Vaginal procedures</strong><strong>  </strong><strong>Abdominal</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Mos</strong><strong>cowitz   procedure</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Vault in place:</strong><strong>Vault Descent </strong></h3>
<p>McCall culdoplasty       SSF</p>
<p>Plication of            - Injury to Pudendal</p>
<ul><li>Vault + cardinalnerve and internal</li></ul>
<p>+ uterosacral pudendal artery</p>
<p>Ligaments.- Difficult to perform</p>
<ul><li>Obliteration of</li></ul>
<p>POD.</p>
<ul><li>Prophylactic incontinence surgery NR.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Corrective procedures:</strong></h3>
<h3><em><strong>Sexually Active/ Short Vagina:</strong></em></h3>
