but may help an individual basis. CVR it may offer better cycle control than COC.There are no data on managing bleeding associated with the patch Continue for at least 3 months as bleeding may settle in this time.<strong>A first-line COC (30-35 μg EE with LNG norethisterone). can be considered for up to 3 months continuously or in the usual cyclical regimen (unlicensed).No evidence that reducing injection interval for DMPA Implies bleeding. However, DMPA may be given after a 10-week IntervalTo reduce the duration of bleeding episodes in DMPA mefenamic acid 500 mg twice (or licensed use up to three times) daily or tranexamic acid four times daily for 5 days may be effective in the short form but confers no long-term effect.A first-line COC (30-35 μg EE with LNG norethisterone). can be considered for up to 3 months continuously or in the usual cyclical regimen (unlicensed).No evidence that reducing injection interval for DMPA Implies bleeding. However, DMPA may be given after a 10-week IntervalTo reduce the duration of bleeding episodes in DMPA mefenamic acid 500 mg twice (or licensed use up to three times) daily or tranexamic acid four times daily for 5 days may be effective in the short form but confers no long-term effect.</strong>A first-line COC (30-35 μg EE with LNG norethisterone). can be considered for up to 3 months continuously or in the usual cyclical regimen (unlicensed).No evidence that reducing injection interval for DMPA Implies bleeding. However, DMPA may be given after a 10-week IntervalTo reduce the duration of bleeding episodes in DMPA mefenamic acid 500 mg twice (or licensed use up to three times) daily or tranexamic acid four times daily for 5 days may be effective in the short form but confers no long-term effect.A first-line COC (30-35 μg EE with LNG norethisterone). can be considered for up to 3 months continuously or in the usual cyclical regimen (unlicensed).No evidence that reducing injection interval for DMPA Implies bleeding. However, DMPA