<p>Rule out Ectopic</p>
<p>&amp; refer to GTD center.</p>
<h3><strong>GTN after Non – molar Pregnancy:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>UPT should be performed in all cases of persistent / irregular bleeding after pregnancy last &gt;8weeks.</li><li>Symptoms of metastatic disease, dyspnea, hemoptysis, seizures.</li><li>Biopsy from vagina is not recommended.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>GTD center Referral:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Stable incomplete evacuation.</li><li>ed β – HCG after 2 doses of metho after PUL.</li><li>ed β – HCG after ruling out Ectopic.</li><li>All twin GTD.</li><li>All PSTT, ETT.<strong>Register </strong><strong>@</strong></li><li>Atypical PSN.<strong>GTD</strong></li><li>Complete/partial mole.<strong>center</strong></li><li>Limited macroscopic / microscopic</li><li>Molar changes.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Twin – Molar:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Referral to FMU for invasive testing and karyotyping.</li><li>1 molar and 1 viable fetus.</li><li>Diagnostic doubt.</li><li>Rule out partial mole.</li><li>Placental Hyperplasia</li><li>Counselling regarding perinatal mortality.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Risks in Twin Molar:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Early fetal loss – 40%.</li><li>PTB – 36%.</li><li>PE – 20%.</li><li>Babies surviving 51%.</li><li>No maternal death</li><li>no increased need for chemo.</li></ul>
<p><strong>PSTT, ETT</strong> referral to GTD Centre.</p>
<ul><li>Role of Hysterectomy &amp; intensive chemo.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>PSN:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Atypical</li><li>Called up to centre for discussion.</li><li>Staging.</li><li>Typical.</li><li>No further investigation.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Follow up</strong><strong> after molar pregnancy</strong><strong> (individualized)</strong></h3>
<p>Complete:                   partial mole.   Previous molar</p>
<p>pregnancy but</p>
<p>not required chemo.</p>
<p>β – HCG                    till 2 consecutives</p>
<p>Returns to                  normal – HCG</p>
<p>Normal                       4weeks apart.</p>
<p>No need of</p>
<p>follow up in</p>
<p>Within 56After 56subsequent</p>
<p>DaysDayspregnancy event.</p>
<p>Total 6m06m0 from normalization.</p>
<h3><strong>GTN =&gt; Choriocarcinoma.</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Raised HCG after evacuation of mole =&gt; No need for h/P.</li><li>Diagnosis is otherwise on H/P.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Investigations:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>CT abdomen (with contrast) + chest</li><li>MRI (with contest) head, pelvis</li><li>HCG</li><li>Pelvic doppler.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>t/m:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>PSTT, ETT (0.2% of GTN) – less sensitive to chemoSurgery is offered.</li><li>Rest of the tumors – chemo is offered.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>FIGO SCARING:</strong></em></h3>', 2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-77d3c175', 't-mm-07-004', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td><em><strong>PARAMETER</strong></em></td><td><em><strong>0</strong></em></td><td><em><strong>1</strong></em></td><td><em><strong>2</strong></em></td><td><em><strong>4</strong></em></td></tr><tr><td>Age</td><td>&lt;40</td><td>&gt; 40</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Antecedent pregnancy</td><td>Mole</td><td>Abortion</td><td>Birth</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Interval from end of index pregnancy to t/m</td><td>&lt;4m`</td><td>4 – 6mo</td><td>7 – 12m</td><td>13 &amp; above</td></tr><tr><td>Pre t/m β – HCG</td><td>&lt;103</td><td>103 - &lt;104</td><td>104 – 105</td><td>&gt;  105</td></tr><tr><td>Largest tumor size</td><td>Up to 2cm</td><td>3 – 4cm</td><td>5 or above</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Size of Mets</td><td>lung</td><td>spleen</td><td>GI</td><td>liver</td></tr><tr><td>No  of Mets</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>1 – 4</td><td>5 – 8</td><td>9 or above</td></tr><tr><td>Previous failed chemo</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Single agent</td><td>Multi agent</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-00f509a0', 't-mm-07-004', 'html', '<h3><strong>Score:</strong></h3>
<p><em><strong>Up to 6 – single Agent.</strong></em></p>
<ul><li>I / M metho alternating folinic acid for 1 week.</li><li>Followed by 6 days’ rest.</li><li>100% cure</li></ul>
<p><em><strong>7 or more – I/V </strong></em><em><strong>multi-Agent</strong></em><em><strong>.</strong></em></p>
<ul><li>Metho, Dactinomycin, etoposide, cyclophosphamide, vincristine.</li><li>Cure 94 %.</li><li><strong>Score </strong><strong>&gt;13:</strong> Risk of.</li><li>Early Death within 3 weeks’ d/t organ bleeding</li><li>Late death due to effects of chemo</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> till 6 consecutive weeks after normalization of β – HCG.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>PSTT, ETT:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Rarest form, 0.2% of GTN.</li><li>Interval between pregnancy &amp; presentation.</li><li>  &gt;48m0 - 100% death.</li><li>  &lt;48m0 - survive.</li><li>Stage 1 - Hysterectomy.</li><li>Chemo – if interval &gt;48m0 platinum based.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Continue </strong><strong>Contraception:</strong></h3>
<p>Don’t require chemoRequiring chemo</p>
<p>Until F/U is complete         1year after completion</p>
<p>of chemo</p>
<ul><li><strong>-   Antecedent mole</strong><strong> and</strong><strong> </strong><strong>risk in </strong><strong>Current pregnancy</strong><strong>    </strong></li></ul>
<p>Risk of PTB</p>
<ul><li><strong>  -  </strong><strong>Risk of</strong><strong> chemo in next pregnancy</strong><strong>:</strong></li></ul>
<p>1. Miscarriage.</p>
<p>2. Anomalies 1.8%</p>
<p>3. Still Birth.</p>
<ul><li><strong>-</strong>   <strong>Mole </strong><strong>followed by</strong><strong> </strong><strong>h</strong><strong>ealthy pregnancy</strong><strong> =&gt;</strong><strong>risk in subsequent pregnancy</strong></li></ul>
<p>LGA + Still birth.</p>
<h3><strong>Risks of chemo:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Successful pregnancy after chemo 80%.</li><li>Premature menopause.</li><li>13% @ 40 years.</li><li>36% @ 45 years.</li><li>Periods are stopped during t/m – restarts after few weeks.</li><li>Risk of 2nd cancer after chemo is low.</li><li>HRT once β HCG is normal</li><li>Estrogen once β HCG is normal</li><li>Fertility drugs once β HCG is normal</li></ul>
<p><strong>Recurrence:</strong> 1% after complete mole</p>', 4) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, "order", is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-07-005', 'chap-mm-07-01', '5. MANAGEMENT OF NAUSEA AND VOMITING IN PREGNANCY AND HYPEREMESIS GRAVIDARUM', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 5. MANAGEMENT OF NAUSEA AND VOMITING IN PREGNANCY AND HYPEREMESIS GRAVIDARUM.', 5, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, description=EXCLUDED.description, is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-e2b098ec', 't-mm-07-005', 'html', '<ul><li>NVP = 90 % of pregnancies.</li><li>Onset before 16 weeks</li><li>HG = 0.3 – 3.6% (Severe form of NVP)</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Mechanism:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Hypersensitivity to vomiting hormone growth differentiation factor 15 IGDF – 15</li><li>HCG</li><li>Genetic predisposition.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Diagnosis of NVP</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Onset: 4 -7 weeks</li><li>Peak: 9 weeks.</li><li>Settles: 20 weeks in 90% women.</li><li>Rule out other causes.</li><li>Onset must be before 16 weeks.</li></ul>
<p>Onset after 10+6 weeks =&gt; less likely NVP.</p>
<h3><strong>HG:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Severe NVP affecting daily activity</li><li>Inability to eat or drink</li><li>Dehydration.</li><li>Ketonuria is no longer used</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Severity of NVP</strong></h3>
<p>1.Objective and validated index</p>
<p>2.PUQE SCORE</p>
<ul><li>PUQE index also track response to treatment for mild &amp; moderate but not severe and HG</li></ul>
<p>3.HELP – can be used to track response to treatment in severe NV and HG.</p>
<ul><li><strong>PUQE score(24</strong><strong>HRS</strong><strong>):</strong></li><li>Mild = up to 6.</li><li>Moderate = 7 – 12.</li><li>Severe = 13 – 15.</li></ul>', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
