<p><strong>LOWER RISKEarly Mobilization and avoidance of dehydration.LOWER RISKEarly Mobilization and avoidance of dehydration.</strong><strong>LOWER RISK</strong>Early Mobilization and avoidance of dehydration.<strong>LOWER RISK</strong>Early Mobilization and avoidance of dehydration.</p>
<h3><strong>LMWH:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Agent of choice.</li><li>Risk of bleeding &lt; 2%.</li><li>Dose according to recent weight.</li><li>No platelet monitoring as minimal risk of HIT.</li><li>No anti X – a monitoring required.</li><li>Safe in B.F.</li><li>Decrease   Dose in renal impairment.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Creatinine</strong><strong> clearance</strong> - &lt;30ml / min.</p>
<p>Enoxa / delta &lt; 30 ml / min.     Low dose should</p>
<p>Tinzaparin &lt; 20ml / min.be given.</p>
<h3><strong>Prophylactic Doses: </strong></h3>', 5) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-53f00d1c', 't-mm-08-003', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Weight + 40</strong></td><td><strong>Enoxaparin + 20</strong></td><td><strong>D</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>ltaparin + 2500</strong></td><td><strong>Tinzapar</strong><strong>inn</strong></td></tr><tr><td>&lt; 50kg</td><td>20mg</td><td>2500 units</td><td>3500 units</td></tr><tr><td>50 – 90</td><td>40</td><td>5000</td><td>4500</td></tr><tr><td>91 – 130</td><td>60mg</td><td>75000</td><td>7000</td></tr><tr><td>&gt;130</td><td>80</td><td>10,000</td><td>9000</td></tr><tr><td>High prophylactic dose<br/>50 – 90 kg</td><td>40mg B.D</td><td>5000 B.D</td><td>4500 B.D</td></tr></tbody></table>', 6) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-b04447c3', 't-mm-08-003', 'html', '<h3><strong>C/I of LMWH:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Known Bleeding disorder.</li><li>Active A/N or P/P bleeding.</li><li>Major Hge (previous).</li><li>Plt &lt; 75 x 109.</li><li>Acute stroke in previous 4 weeks.</li><li>(both ischemic &amp; Haemorrhagic).</li><li>Severe Renal disease GFR &lt; 30.</li><li>Severe liver disease</li><li>Uncontrolled HTN &gt; 200/120.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>UFH:</strong></h3>
<h3><em>Indications:</em></h3>
<ul><li>In women @ very high risk of Thrombosis.</li><li>In peripartum period where    ed risk of Hge or where Anaesthesia is required.</li><li>Plt monitoring every 2 – 3 days from 4 – 14day of treatment until heparin is stopped.</li><li>Modifiable.</li><li>Complete reversal with protamine sulfate.</li><li>Stop 4 hours before regional Anaesthesia.</li><li>Less neuraxial hematoma.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Fondaparinux, Danapar</strong><strong>oid:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Given to women Intolerant to heparin.</li><li>T ½ -= 24 hours avoid regional anaesthesia</li><li>used in conjunction with haematologist.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Warfarin:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em>Indications</em></li><li>Mechanical heart valve.</li><li>switch to LMWH 2 weeks after missed period (6 – 12 weeks).</li><li>Stop @ 36 weeks.</li><li>Restart after 5 – 7 days of delivery.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Dextran:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Avoid in pregnancy.</li><li>Anaphylactic reactions.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Oral Thrombin &amp; x – a </strong><strong>inhibitors</strong><strong>. </strong></h3>
<ul><li>NOACS: Non vitamin K antagonist oral anticoagulants.</li><li>Avoided in pregnancy and breast feeding</li><li>Dabigatran, rivaroxaban, apixaban.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Anti – embolism Stockings:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>14 – 15 mmHg in pregnancy/ puerperium in hospital where LMWH is C/I.</li><li>Most VTE in pregnancy are iliofemoral.</li><li>Post C/S combined with LMWH.</li><li>Long distance travel &gt; 4hours.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Graduated compre</strong><strong>ssion Stockings:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Post embolism/ post thrombotic syndrome.</li></ul>', 7) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
