<p>good NPV but no positive predictive value.good NPV but no positive predictive value.good NPV but no positive predictive value.good NPV but no positive predictive value.</p>
<h3><strong>VZV: Human Herpesvirus 3:</strong></h3>
<p><em><strong>Maternal Effects.</strong></em></p>
<ul><li>Pneumonia, hepatitis, encephalitis.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Fetal </strong></em><em><strong>varicella syndrome (</strong></em><em><strong>FVS</strong></em><em><strong>)</strong></em><em><strong>:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Eye defects.</li><li>Limb hypoplasia.</li><li>Neurological abnormalities.</li><li>Skin scarring.</li><li>(VZV – reactivation).</li><li>Sphincter dysfunction.</li><li>Cortical atrophy.</li></ul>
<p><em><strong>Neonatal</strong></em><em><strong>.</strong></em></p>
<ul><li>Neonatal varicella syndrome</li><li>Pneumonia</li><li>Sepsis</li><li>meningitis</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Hospital Assessment:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Neurological symptoms.</li><li>Respiratory symptoms – smoking + cough.</li><li>Haemorrhagic rash.</li><li>Immuno compromised taking steroids &gt; 3m0.</li><li>2nd half of pregnancy even without complication.</li><li>Severe symptomshospital admission:</li><li>Isolation.</li><li>MDT</li></ul>
<p>Obstetrician.</p>
<p>FMU.</p>
<p>Neonatologist.</p>
<p>Virologist.</p>
<ul><li><strong>if delivery occurs within 7 days:</strong></li><li>Neonatal VZIG + Acyclovir.</li><li>For PEP</li><li>When neonate has rash =&gt; Acyclovir</li><li><strong>Maternal shingles @ delivery.</strong></li><li>Baby delivers.</li><li>No IVIG required.</li><li><strong>Maternal shingles P/P.</strong></li><li>Give IVIG .</li></ul>', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO topics (id, chapter_id, title, description, "order", is_published, author, source) VALUES ('t-mm-09-004', 'chap-mm-09-01', '1.3. HIV IN PREGNANCY', 'Detailed medical reference and study guide on 1.3. HIV IN PREGNANCY.', 4, true, 'Dr. Farzana Muneer', 'Maternal Mind FCPS/MRCOG Textbook') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, description=EXCLUDED.description, is_published=true;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-56613801', 't-mm-09-004', 'html', '<ul><li><strong>MDT + Peer support.</strong></li><li>Mental health assessment @:</li><li>Booking.</li><li>4 – 6 weeks postnatal.</li><li>3 – 4m0 postnatal.</li><li>Sexual health screening:</li><li>Recommended in newly diagnosed.</li><li>Suggested in previously diagnosed.</li><li>Monitoring &amp; testing:</li><li><em><strong>HIV Resistance</strong></em> – all pts before treatment except late presenters after 28 weeks.</li><li><em><strong>CD4:</strong></em> &gt; 350 cells/mm0.</li><li>Base line</li><li>Delivery</li><li>Before initiation of treatment.</li><li><em><strong>Viral load:</strong></em></li><li>2 – 4 weeks after treatment commencement.</li><li>Once in each trimester.</li><li>@ 36 weeks.</li><li>@ delivery.</li><li><em><strong>LFT’S:</strong></em></li><li>Before CART.</li><li>@ each routine blood test.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Persistent</strong><strong> viral road:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>50 HIV copies look for followings.</li><li>concomitant medication.</li><li>Compliance.</li><li>Perform resistance testing.</li><li>Drug monitoring.</li><li>Optimize best regimen.</li><li>Consider intensification.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Women </strong><strong>conceive</strong><strong> on CART.</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Continued CART except:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Non standard regimen like protease inhibitor monotherapy.</li><li>Darunavir/ Cobi stat.</li><li>Elvitegravir.            Low pharmacokinetics</li><li>Raltegravir – in divided dosing 400 B.D instead of 1200 OD.</li><li>Dolutegravir – NTD after 8 weeks can be given.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Not on CART when to start (all women by 24 weeks).</strong></h3>
<p>Viral load &gt;100,000.30,000 – 100,000    &lt; 300,000</p>
<p>OR CD4 &lt; 200.</p>
<p>1st 2nd  early      as soon as     possible in</p>', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
