INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-4cd0d8e2', 't-mm-09-015', 'html', '<h3><strong>Role of immunoglobulins:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>I/V immunoglobulins should be considering as part of treatment for G positive and Toxic Shock Syndrome when other measure are failing.</li><li>Not effective for G negative or sepsis in general.</li><li>Limited use in sickest women</li><li>Use in critical care setting.</li><li>Use where blood warning device available.</li><li>Clindamycin + IVIG are reported synergistic and beneficial</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>C/I:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>Congenital immunoglobulins A deficiency.</li></ul>
<h3><em><strong>Dose:</strong></em></h3>
<ul><li>2g/kg.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Fetal monitoring:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Expedite birth in critically ill women if it is beneficial.</li><li>Decision by senior obstetrician after discussion with women and/ or family.</li><li>Preterm birth:</li><li>Mgso4 and steroids should be considered.</li><li>CEFM.</li><li>Risk of neonatal encephalopathy and CP is    ed in case of I/U infection.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Neonatal Care:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Babies of women treated for sepsis during labor or within 24 hours before or after birth should be assessed for neonatal infection.</li><li>If either women or baby is infected with GAS disease in post – partum period, both should be treated with Antibiotics.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Infection control strategies:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>All women after birth should be informed about signs and symptoms of genital tract infection, (written + verbal) + guidance regarding hygiene, hand washing &amp; seeking help when feel unwell.</li><li>All women identified with GAS infection during pregnancy should be aggressively treated.</li><li>All close contact with GAS infected women should seek medical advice &amp; if symptoms develops should be treated with A/B.</li><li>All healthcare professionals who are exposed to respiratory secretions of GAS infected women should be considered for A/B.</li><li>Women with GAS infected should be cared by barrier nursing including clothing, masks, limited mobility.</li><li>Early investigations if suspected</li><li>Take into account the normal physiological changes in labor like    ed HR</li><li>Recognize that sepsis in labor has higher risk of illness or death.</li><li>MDT for sepsis in labor.</li><li>Senior obstetrician</li><li>Senior obstetrician anesthetist</li><li>Senior midwife</li><li>Labor ward coordinator</li><li>Senior neonatologist</li><li>Senior microbiologist</li><li>Include senior intensivist if a woman in labor with sepsis has any of the following sign of organ dysfunction</li><li>1. Altered consciousness</li><li>2. Hypotension (systolic B.P &lt; 90mmHg)</li><li>3. Reduced UOP (&lt; 0.5ml/kg per hour)</li><li>4. Need for 40% oxygen to maintain oxygen saturation above 92%.</li><li>5. Tympanic temperature of &lt; 360C.</li><li>Women with sepsis in labor should have</li><li>1. Clear and agreed MDT care plan</li><li>2. Documentation of Plan</li><li>3. Regular review of Plan according to clinical picture</li><li>Involve women and her partner in her care plan and any intervention</li><li>Discuss mode and timing of delivery by taking account of</li><li>DOP</li><li>Fetal well – being</li><li>Source of sepsis if known</li><li>Parity</li><li>Stage and progress of labor</li><li>Response to treatment</li><li>Expedite birth if source is genital tract.</li><li><strong>Anesthesia</strong> – regional anesthesia with caution after consultant advice.</li><li><strong>Analg</strong><strong>esia in labo</strong><strong>u</strong><strong>r:</strong></li><li>Regional analgesia with caution after consultant advice</li><li>Birthing pool after senior obstetrician or senior midwife’s discussion.</li><li>Antibiotics before inserting the needle of regional analgesia</li><li>MDT review regarding pain relief every 4 hours.</li><li><strong>Fetal Monitoring</strong> – continuous</li><li><strong>antimicrobial drugs</strong></li><li>Send culture before giving antimicrobial</li><li>Start broad spectrum empirical therapy after sending culture.</li><li>Choice of antibiotics according to local antimicrobial guidelines.</li><li><strong>Post - natal care</strong></li><li>MDT within 24 hours of birth</li><li>MDT discussion includes</li><li>1. Specimens for culture</li><li>2. Antimicrobial treatment</li></ul>', 10) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
