INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-d3f3d080', 't-mm-10-034', 'html', '<h3><strong>I</strong><strong>ntrapartum</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>1. Prolong 1st stage</li><li>2. Secondary arrest</li><li>3. Prolong 2nd stage</li><li>4. Oxytocin augmentation</li><li>5. Assisted vaginal delivery.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Diagnosis:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Difficulty with delivery of face and chin</li><li>Turtle neck sign</li><li>Failure of restitution</li><li>Failure of shoulder to descend</li><li>Axial traction can be used</li><li>Lateral and any other avoided =&gt; nerve avulsion injury</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Prevention</strong></h3>
<ul><li>IOL</li><li>Don’t prevent in non-diabetic macrosomia</li><li>Prevent SD in diabetic macrosomia</li><li>Elective C/S consider in DM + EFW &gt; 4.5kg</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Post-natal Management of women/ New Born:</strong></h3>
<h3><strong>Maternal risks:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>PPH 11%</li><li>Perineal tear (3rd/4th degree) 38%</li><li>Vaginal, cervical laceration</li><li>Bladder rupture</li><li>Uterine rupture</li><li>Symphysial separation</li><li>Sacra iliac joint dislocation</li><li>Lateral femoral cutaneous neuropathy</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Fetal risks:</strong></h3>', 5) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-b216df09', 't-mm-10-034', 'heading', '1. BPI – 2.3 – 16%,', 6) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-e45c0ba3', 't-mm-10-034', 'html', '<ul><li>46% of BPI due to substandard care.</li><li>10% permanent injury to nerve, 4% during C/S and 12% after simple C/S.</li><li>Always document the anterior shoulder as posterior shoulder is never because of health care professionals’ undue traction, post shoulder is always affected by maternal effort</li><li>2. Humerus facture.</li><li>3. Clavicle fracture.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Recurrence:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>10 times higher = 1 – 25%</li><li>Either c/s or vaginal birth – joint decision between women and her carer</li></ul>
<h3>Call for help:</h3>
<ul><li>Midwife coordinator for documentation, time of SD, arrival of doctor, performance of maneuver, which shoulder is anterior.</li><li>Additional midwife help</li><li>Neonatologist and</li><li>1st line1st line1st line1st lineDiscourage pushing it exacerbate shoulder impactionAvoid fundal pressure Risk of uterine ruptureDiscourage pushing it exacerbate shoulder impactionAvoid fundal pressure Risk of uterine ruptureDiscourage pushing it exacerbate shoulder impactionAvoid fundal pressure Risk of uterine ruptureDiscourage pushing it exacerbate shoulder impactionAvoid fundal pressure Risk of uterine ruptureAnesthetist</li></ul>
<p>MC – Robert’s position thighs to abd 90% successful</p>
<ul><li>Suprapubic pressure rocking/ continuous</li><li>Routine axial traction 90% success</li><li>Episiotomy as it will make internal maneuver easier</li><li>Try either maneuver 1st – depending up clinical situation and operator experienceInform consultant obs and anesthetistFailedTry either maneuver 1st – depending up clinical situation and operator experienceInform consultant obs and anesthetistFailedTry either maneuver 1st – depending up clinical situation and operator experienceInform consultant obs and anesthetistFailedTry either maneuver 1st – depending up clinical situation and operator experienceInform consultant obs and anesthetistFailedIf patient is less mobile and have epiduralPost aspect of ant shoulder and post aspect of post shoulderIf patient is less mobile and have epiduralPost aspect of ant shoulder and post aspect of post shoulderIf patient is less mobile and have epiduralPost aspect of ant shoulder and post aspect of post shoulderIf patient is less mobile and have epiduralPost aspect of ant shoulder and post aspect of post shoulder</li></ul>
<p>Internal rotatory maneuversInternal rotatory maneuversInternal rotatory maneuversInternal rotatory maneuversDelivery of posterior armDelivery of posterior armDelivery of posterior armDelivery of posterior arm</p>
<p>2nd line2nd line2nd line2nd line</p>
