<p><strong>Extradural chignon:</strong> Temporary swelling @ vacuum cup application site.</p>
<h3><strong>Maternal Outcomes:</strong></h3>', 6) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-cd232480', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>Vacuum</strong></td><td><strong>Forceps</strong></td><td><strong>Sequential</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Episiotomy</td><td>50 – 60</td><td>90%</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>VV tear</td><td>10%</td><td>20 %</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>OASI</td><td>1 – 4%</td><td>8 – 12%</td><td>17.4%</td></tr><tr><td>PPH</td><td>10 – 40%</td><td>10 – 40%</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Incontinence</td><td>Common @ 6 weeks improve with time</td></tr></tbody></table>', 7) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-e1b80959', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<h3><strong>Fetal Outcomes:</strong></h3>', 8) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-e2f652b8', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<table><tbody><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>Vacuum</strong></td><td><strong>Forceps</strong></td><td><strong>Sequential</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Cephal haematoma</td><td>1 – 12%</td><td>__</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Facial/ Scalp laceration</td><td>10%</td><td>10%</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Retinal Haemorrhage</td><td>17 – 38%</td><td>Less than vacuum</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Jaundice</td><td>5 – 15%</td><td>5 – 15%</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Subgaleal Haemorrhage</td><td>3 – 6/1000</td><td>__</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>ICH / Subdural</td><td>5-15/10,000</td><td>5-15/10,000</td><td>2 – 3 times more</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical spine injury</td><td>__</td><td>Rare due to Kelland</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Skull fracture</td><td>__</td><td>Rare</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Fascial Nerve pulse</td><td>__</td><td>Rare</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Fetal death</td><td>Very rare</td><td>Very rare</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>', 9) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-dd13dc4c', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<ul><li>Malpractice litigation – failure to discontinue</li><li>Serious neonatal injuries – excessive pulls &gt;3 with forceps and prolong application - &gt;12min.</li><li>Paired cord sample after all attempts @ AVB</li><li>Incident reporting: failed AVB, SD, PPH, OASI, Neonatal problems</li><li><strong>ODON Device</strong> under trial</li><li>Head dis-impaction before/ in advance C/S =&gt; GPP</li><li>Episiotomy – discuss</li><li>routine – Nulliparous and Forceps.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Care after AVB:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Single dose of Ampicillin and clavulanic acid =&gt; Recommended after AVB</li><li>Hygiene</li><li>NSAIDs and Paracetamol routinely</li><li>Risk of urinary retention so inform regarding Bladder emptying</li><li>Urinary retention =&gt; post-void volume</li><li>Physiotherapy @ 3m0 offer to reduce urinary incontinence (38 – 31%)</li><li>Indwelling catheter 6 – 12 hours after AVB in regional anesthesia.</li><li>Post – traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) assessment of symptoms @ 1m0 and referral to skilled professionals.</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Future Birth:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>More chances of spontaneous labour after AVB (80% after AVB and 30% after 2nd stage C/S).</li><li>3RD AND 4th degree tear individual care plan in upcoming deliveries.</li></ul>', 10) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-b80fb749', 't-mm-10-036', 'heading', '13. INDUCTION OF LABOUR: IOL', 11) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-1f8a11a4', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<ul><li>1/5 pregnancies need IOL</li><li>2/3 give birth without intervention</li><li>15% need AVB</li><li>22% end up in C/S</li><li>Most women go into labour by 42 weeks</li><li>@ 38 weeks all women should be offered information regarding</li></ul>
<p>1. Risk of pregnancies that last longer than 42 weeks.</p>
<p>2. Expectant management</p>
<p>3. Membranes stripping</p>
<ul><li>Method</li><li>benefits of spontaneous labour</li><li>Uncomfortable, pain</li><li>Possible bleeding</li></ul>', 12) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-1cbbb0bf', 't-mm-10-036', 'heading', '4. IOL between 41 – 42 weeks', 13) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, "order") VALUES ('cb-dcd23fb3', 't-mm-10-036', 'html', '<h3><strong>Information giving before IOL:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>1. Reason</li><li>2. When, where, how</li><li>3. Support, pain relief</li><li>4. Alternative to IOL</li><li>5. Risk/ Benefits of IOL</li><li>6. what if IOL fails</li><li>7. prolong pregnancy IOL between 41 – 42 weeks exact timing according to patient’s wishes patient who decline =&gt; after 42 weeks</li><li>CTG + Amniotic Fluid =&gt; twice/ week</li><li>PPROM</li><li>Before 37 weeks expectant management, to prolong till 37 weeks. In case of fetomaternal indications offer IOL</li><li>PROM =&gt; 24 hours after ROM offer IOL</li><li>Previous CS – PG E2/ expectant according to women wishes, explain risk of rupture and emergency CS</li><li>Maternal request @ or after 40 weeks =&gt; under special conditions</li><li>Breech – Not recommended</li><li>Severe IUGR + compromise NR</li><li>History of precipitated labor – not routinely offered.</li><li>IUD</li><li>Patient physically Offer a choice of</li><li>wellexpectant/ IOL by</li><li>No infectionmifepristone, FPG E2</li><li>No bleeding or misoprostol.</li><li>Unwell</li><li>+ bleeding + infectionIOL</li><li>Ruptured management</li><li>IUD + previous</li><li>CS =&gt; risk of rupture, reduce dose of MISO</li><li>Fetal macrosomia =&gt; Discuss</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Methods:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Sweeping of Membranes = Adjunct to IOL</li><li>primigravida = 40 – 41weeks</li><li>Multigravida = 41 weeks</li><li>additional sweeping can be done if patient don’t go into labor.</li><li>Bishop = &gt; 8 =&gt; Favorable</li><li>MISO, MEFI =&gt; IUD only</li><li>PG E2</li><li>Tablets – 3mg6 hourly -</li><li>GEL – 2mg2 doses.</li><li>Pessary – 20mg =&gt; 24 hours – 1 dose</li><li>Amniotomy + synto =&gt; only if risk of hyper stimulation</li></ul>
<h3><strong>IOL @ older </strong><strong>women</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<p>Age @ delivery beyond 35 years    ed from 8 – 20% and @ 40 years 1.2 – 3.6%</p>
<h3><strong>Risk</strong><strong> </strong><strong> </strong><strong>  </strong><strong>with age</strong><strong>:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>APH – PPH</li><li>Abruption</li><li>PTL</li><li>Post dated</li><li>Unexplained S.B</li><li>DM</li><li>HTN</li><li>IUGR – LBW</li><li>Previa</li><li>CS and OVB</li><li>Neonatal Mortality – 1.3time.</li><li>SB @ Term</li><li>40 years – 2/1000</li><li>&lt; 40 yeas – 1/1000</li><li>So, IOL @ 39 – 40 weeks if age &gt; 40 years</li><li>Discussion with women</li><li>SB @ 41 weeks</li><li>35 years – 0.75/1000</li><li>40 years – 2.5/1000</li></ul>
<h3><strong>CEFM vs Intermittent in IOL</strong></h3>
<ul><li>No difference in CP and perinatal mortality</li><li>½ the chances of neonatal seizures</li><li>Risk of C/S</li><li>Risk of AVB</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Setting and timing of IOL:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>Morning time – high patient satisfaction</li><li>OPD/ In patient</li><li>If support is in place</li><li>Continuously audited.</li></ul>
<p>Monitoring</p>
<ul><li>Before inductionAfter Induction</li><li>CTG -<strong> CEFM</strong></li><li>   Bishop                        once contractions</li><li>Begun</li><li><strong>- </strong><strong>Bishop</strong></li><li>24 hours after pessary.6 hours afterGel/Tablets orwhen contractionsbegun.</li><li>Normal/ Reasoning FHR</li><li>Intermittent monitoring</li></ul>
<h3><strong>OPD IOL:</strong></h3>
<ul><li><em>Return</em><em> to hospital</em><em> if:</em></li><li>Contractions begun or</li><li>No contractions after 6 hours</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Pain relief:</strong></h3>
<ul><li>IOL is more painful</li><li>Offer variety of pain relief</li><li>Self – coping</li><li>Simple Analgesia</li><li>Continuous supports</li><li>Epidural</li><li>Water Birth</li></ul>
<h3><strong>Prevention &amp; management of complications:</strong></h3>
<p>UterineFailed IOLCordUterine</p>
<p>Hyper          prolapse.   rupture.</p>
<p>Stimulation</p>
<p>Tocolysisdiscuss-Avoid    - Em C/S    after evaluationamniotomyeither@ high headrepeat IOL    - Avoid upward              or C/S        pushing.</p>', 14) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET content=EXCLUDED.content, type=EXCLUDED.type;
